<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#census">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Census</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">A census is an official count of a population, often recording households, property and obligations. Censuses enabled states to assess taxes and military service, as in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a> and the record-keeping of the Macedonian and Seleucid empires. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/qing-empire">Qing Empire</a>'s banner system also functioned as a census mechanism for its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchus">Manchu</a> population.</p></div>
